      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "If we compare with regular C#, its possible to call public methods from a disabled script.  I think this is intended behavior. \n\nSee: https://discussions.unity.com/t/call-a-public-function-of-a-disabled-monobehaviour-script-still-work/147054",
